{# A module page written by somebody who printed the time on the server.

   Four drifts, one per assertion: a date printed with no element around it, a
   `<time>` with no machine instant in it, a shape the frame does not answer, and
   a relative label whose title carries a FORMATTED date rather than the machine
   instant — the same defect one attribute further in.

   The last line is the relative-label idiom written correctly, and it is here so
   the checks are watched ACCEPTING it: a duration is right in every zone, so it
   is not a `<time>` and is not rewritten.

   The comment itself prints {{ x|date('c') }} as prose, which is not markup and
   must not be read as any of them. #}
<div class="page">
    <p>Recorded {{ patrol.endedAt|date('j F Y H:i') }}.</p>
    <time data-localtime-format="stamp">7 sep · 08:41</time>
    <time datetime="{{ patrol.startedAt|date('c') }}" data-localtime-format="timestamp">7 sep · 08:41</time>
    <span title="{{ patrol.startedAt|date('j F Y') }}">3 days ago</span>
    <span title="{{ patrol.endedAt|date('c') }}">6 min ago</span>
</div>
